Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.37,0:00:02.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Remember the budget of the shoebox.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.65,0:00:06.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Snapshot by snapshot,\Nenergy rises or falls.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.05,0:00:12.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Only the crowd balances, on average,\Nlike a bank account over the years.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.08,0:00:15.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Now, a tempting fix for the machine.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.21,0:00:22.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Force every generated snapshot to balance\Nits budget exactly. Better, or worse?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.68,0:00:27.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Worse.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.83,0:00:31.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Push each snapshot until\Nits energy stops changing:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.70,0:00:35.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}the wide pile collapses\Ninto a spike at zero.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.69,0:00:38.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}A ledger where every single day balances.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.25,0:00:41.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}No real account looks like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.19,0:00:45.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The {\c&H00A1ED&}distribution distance{\c&HF7F4F2&}\Nto the truth grows ninefold.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.35,0:00:49.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}A short proof says why:\Neven a perfect generator,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.79,0:00:52.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}forced this way, cannot match the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.30,0:00:55.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}So the budget goes on the crowd shelf.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.12,0:01:00.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}On the next test bench, a cruder\Nscore is fooled by such a spike.
